/* ---------------- Mask-aware coarsening (gap 18) ----------------------------
 * cfd coarsens three things with three DIFFERENT rules, and they are not interchangeable
 * (cfd.html:862, :880, :897):
 *
 *   solid mask      a coarse cell is solid iff ALL 8 children are solid   -> 'all'
 *   Dirichlet bits  bitwise OR over the 8 children                        -> 'any-bits'
 *   wall bits       a coarse face is blocked iff ALL 4 fine faces on that side are blocked
 *                                                                         -> 'face-all'
 *
 * The file documents `coarsenSolid` as "the least-bad rule ... it keeps 1-cell channels alive, at
 * the price of letting 1-cell walls leak on coarse levels - which is exactly what the CG wrapper is
 * there to repair." Measured on the CPU replica of that model problem, the naive alternative ('any',
 * coarse cell solid if any child is) costs MGPCG 11 iterations instead of 9 with red-black GS and
 * 22 instead of 13 with damped Jacobi — it closes the 1-cell doorway on the coarse grid. */
export const MULTIGRID_MASK_RULES=Object.freeze(['all','any','any-bits','all-bits','face-all','face-any']);
