/* ---------------- Recorded iteration plans (gap 8, part 2) ------------------
 * A Krylov iteration is the same sequence of dispatches every time; only the buffer contents move.
 * cfd records it once as WGSL pipelines and replays it into ONE encoder, ONE pass, ONE submit
 * (cfd.html:1244-1263). GPUIterationPlan is that shape for the runtime: operations are recorded as
 * closures, and run() replays `iterations` of them into a single GPUCommandBatch per `submitEvery`.
 *
 * What it does and does not buy, stated plainly. It removes SUBMITS and, because every recorded op
 * is a slot op, it removes mapAsync entirely between checks. It does NOT cache bind groups:
 * GPUComputeKernel builds a bind group per dispatch, so the CPU-side encoding cost is paid on every
 * replay. describe().caveat says so. Cutting that too would mean a bind-group cache inside
 * GPUComputeKernel, which is a different change with a different blast radius. */
